    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d776">

                <pb facs="0934" n="922" sameAs="frus:frus1943v03/pg922"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">701.0090/2158a: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        Switzerland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Harrison</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-09-02">September 2,
                        1943</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2154. Exchange vessel <hi rendition="#italic">Gripsholm</hi> sailed from New
                        York<anchor n="20" xml:id="d776-f1"/> for Marmagão via Rio de Janeiro,
                    Montevideo and Port Elizabeth as scheduled on September 2 at 7 a.m. Safe
                        conduct<anchor n="21" xml:id="d776-f2"/> assured by all belligerents.</p>
                <p>Please request Swiss Government to inform Japanese Government for its information
                    and information of all other enemy governments.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d776-f1" n="20" xml:id="d776-f1-content">
                <p>With 1430 tons of food parcels and other relief cargo and 5528 pieces of
                    luggage.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d776-f2" n="21" xml:id="d776-f2-content">
                <p>For text of announcement of safe conduct, see Department of State <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Bulletin</hi>, October 16, 1943, p. 256.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
